"# RESONATOR: Unsupervised Cognitive Safety for Autoregressive LLMs\n",
"### Google Colab Demo Notebook — Anthropic Fellows Program Application\n",
"Author: Evan / Necessity Labs\n",
"\n",
"This notebook provides a complete research and engineering showcase of RESONATOR, an unsupervised cognitive safety mechanism designed to preemptively detect and remediate generative degeneration (such as repeating loops and limit cycles) in Autoregressive Large Language Models.\n",
"\n",
"### 🧠 Science & Technical Concept\n",
"Autoregressive LLM generation is fundamentally a discrete-time dynamical system:\n",
"

$$x_t = f(x_{t-1}, x_{t-2}, \dots, x_{t-k})$$

\n",
"\n",
"When an LLM falls into a repetition loop, the system transitions into a stable limit cycle (an orbit) or a point attractor. RESONATOR implements Critical Slowing Down (CSD) monitoring to detect when the system approaches a critical bifurcation threshold (the repetition loop) before visible failure occurs. It monitors the lag-1 autocorrelation ($AR(1)$) of output token state metrics (such as sliding-window token entropy changes) and pairs this with Orbit Resonance tracking to detect periodic limit cycles.\n",
"\n",
"Once the system's stress crosses a Schmitt Trigger threshold, RESONATOR triggers targeted interventions:\n",
"1. Orbit Penalty: Penalizes the specific tokens forming the repetitive limit cycle.\n",
"2. Point Attractor Penalty: Suppresses dominant points of high-frequency recurrence.\n",
"3. Semantic Anchor Boost: Enhances the log-probabilities of contextual prompt tokens, grounding the model back to the original topic.\n",
"4. Neuromodulation: Dynamically scales up the generation temperature (increasing entropy) to facilitate a chaotic escape from the attractor.\n",
"\n",
"---"
]
},
